{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01917",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.97,
      "end_seconds": 5.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "mm hi doctor I hope I'm not disturbing you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.82,
      "end_seconds": 11.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "that's fine, sit down tell me why you came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.29,
      "end_seconds": 20.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "right, uh, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.85,
      "end_seconds": 25.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.72,
      "end_seconds": 32.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "so So the thing is I've got neck pain after a car crash"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.59,
      "end_seconds": 36.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.64,
      "end_seconds": 53.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.7,
      "text": "probably about a week. Yeah. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I told my wife I'd come today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.63,
      "end_seconds": 63.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is what the pattern is what helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.01,
      "end_seconds": 70.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "it's worse with turning i'd say mild it's a couple of times a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.44,
      "end_seconds": 74.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "any a headache as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.97,
      "end_seconds": 77.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Yes, that started yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.12,
      "end_seconds": 81.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "how strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.9,
      "end_seconds": 97.92,
      "duration_seconds": 15.02,
      "text": "I'd say moderate oh, and shoulder tightness that's been about the same, three days as for shoulder tightness, I'd give it a four, out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.7,
      "end_seconds": 102.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.82,
      "end_seconds": 115.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "nearly done with the readings.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.09,
      "end_seconds": 138.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.86,
      "text": "okay: SpO2 99 percent on room air temp 36.6 degrees and BP is 110 over 70 pulse 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.6,
      "end_seconds": 141.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.65,
      "end_seconds": 144.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "We'll look at it together shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.24,
      "end_seconds": 151.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Let me look at the area I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.62,
      "end_seconds": 153.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.95,
      "end_seconds": 175.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.88,
      "text": "there is muscle tenderness either side of the neck and no tenderness over the bones"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.89,
      "end_seconds": 187.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "thank you, you can get dressed. Any numbness in the arms, weakness or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.68,
      "end_seconds": 190.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "So, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.31,
      "end_seconds": 194.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Has there been any loss of consciousness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.14,
      "end_seconds": 198.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "No loss of consciousness, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.09,
      "end_seconds": 202.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Understood. And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.87,
      "end_seconds": 206.86,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.76,
      "end_seconds": 211.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "so, anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.99,
      "end_seconds": 213.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "nothing there, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.46,
      "end_seconds": 229.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.42,
      "end_seconds": 246.78,
      "duration_seconds": 16.36,
      "text": "let me think I have epilepsy for about ten years. I've had COPD yes. It's the not knowing that gets to me. Actually I've had migraines for five years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.64,
      "end_seconds": 253.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "yes, migraines is known to us, good to have that clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.97,
      "end_seconds": 273.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.93,
      "text": "are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.76,
      "end_seconds": 276.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 277.89,
      "end_seconds": 285.49,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "Actually, I remember he had some kinda reaction to diclofenac before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.71,
      "end_seconds": 288.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "I don't remember that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.14,
      "end_seconds": 299.22,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "alright so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. Tell me about your routine work habits that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.67,
      "end_seconds": 314.96,
      "duration_seconds": 14.29,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day. Nothing, I'm teetotal. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.67,
      "end_seconds": 319.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.5,
      "end_seconds": 325.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Lamotrigine, 100 milligrams, twice a day for the fits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 330.06,
      "end_seconds": 336.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.54,
      "text": "right, that's what's prescribed, but I'm not sure he takes it it every day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.59,
      "end_seconds": 342.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "I'm on Tiotropium inhaler, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.73,
      "end_seconds": 345.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "is that that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.92,
      "end_seconds": 351.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "About a year now. Sumatriptan i take it 50 milligrams, maybe, when needed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.9,
      "end_seconds": 357.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.34,
      "end_seconds": 361.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "no, um, it's at home"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.4,
      "end_seconds": 375.62,
      "duration_seconds": 12.22,
      "text": "okay thinking it through this looks most like whiplash-type neck strain that's my thinking for now and it may change as we learn more another possibility is a cervical spine injury"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.82,
      "end_seconds": 380.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.26,
      "end_seconds": 388.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like whiplash-type neck strain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.94,
      "end_seconds": 413.9,
      "duration_seconds": 11.96,
      "text": "the treatment will be naproxen, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, one week you take it by mouth that should help with neck pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 415.95,
      "end_seconds": 418.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "How soon will it work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 419.96,
      "end_seconds": 440.93,
      "duration_seconds": 20.97,
      "text": "keep your neck moving gently and avoid a collar and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit so we can settle the dose book a review if not better in two weeks so that's all from me any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 441.95,
      "end_seconds": 445.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "right, no, that's all thanks a lot"
    }
  ]
}